IND$FILE                                              MECAFF File Transfer
IND$FILE transfers files between the 3270 terminal and the VM/370 host
using the IND$FILE CUT-mode protocol. It supports both binary and ASCII
text transfers with various record format options.

  Command syntax:
    IND$FILE PUT|GET fn ft fm [ options ]
    IND$FILE TST     fn ft fm [ options ]    (local test mode only)

  Operations:
    PUT    Upload a file from the terminal to the host.
    GET    Download a file from the host to the terminal.
    TST    Test mode: verify symmetric encode/decode of a host file.
           This command runs locally and must not be issued remotely.

  Required parameters:
    fn     CMS file name (1-8 characters).
    ft     CMS file type (1-8 characters).
    fm     CMS file mode (A-Z, or * for accessed disk).

  Options:
    ASCII      Transfer as ASCII text instead of binary.
               When uploading, EBCDIC is converted to ASCII.
               When downloading, ASCII is converted to EBCDIC.
               Lines are trimmed of trailing blanks on download.
    CRLF       Use CR/LF line endings (only valid with ASCII).
               Without this option, LF line endings are used.
               Lines shorter than LRECL are padded with spaces.
    APPEND     Append to an existing file instead of overwriting.
    RECFM V    Use variable-length records (default).
    RECFM F    Use fixed-length records, padded to LRECL.
    LRECL nn   Set the logical record length to nn (1-255).
               Default is 80. Fixed records are padded to this
               length; variable records wrap at this length.
    MAP name   Use a custom character mapping from file
               'name IND$MAP *'. This overrides default EBCDIC
               character remappings.
    DUMP       Dump additional diagnostic information during
               transfers. For troubleshooting only.

  Examples:
    IND$FILE GET MYFILE TXT A ASCII
    IND$FILE PUT DATA TXT A ASCII CRLF LRECL 132
    IND$FILE GET BINPROG EXE A
    IND$FILE PUT NOTES TXT A ASCII APPEND RECFM V

  Notes:
    - Binary transfers (without ASCII) preserve all bytes as-is
      and do not perform line-end conversion or blank trimming.
    - ASCII transfers convert between ASCII and EBCDIC using the
      standard IBM code page. Character remapping files (IND$MAP)
      can override specific character pairs.
    - When uploading ASCII text with CRLF, lines that fill the
      full LRECL width are written as a single record without
      generating a spurious empty trailing record.
    - Fixed-length records (RECFM F) shorter than LRECL are
      padded with spaces (ASCII) or nulls (binary).
    - The TST command performs a round-trip encode/decode test
      on a file already on the host, reporting any mismatches.

  Error codes:
    TRANS03  File transfer complete.
    TRANS04  File transfer complete, records were segmented.
    TRANS06  Command incomplete or invalid option.
    TRANS16  Incorrect request code (invalid PUT/GET/TST).
    TRANS17  Invalid file name or record format.
    TRANS34  CMS file not found or error accessing file.
    TRANS35  CMS disk is read-only.
    TRANS37  CMS disk is full.
    TRANS99  Protocol error, conversion error, or internal error.
